{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.GbDepthPeriodCorrespondence","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.GbDepthPeriodCorrespondence","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.HopfAlgebra.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.NumberTheory.NumberField.Basic"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.GBDepthPeriodCorrespondence.depth_period_nonempty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.GBDepthPeriodCorrespondence.depth_period_nonempty","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gb-depth-period-correspondence.lean#L147-L159","doc":"**Conditional (downstream of the keystone).** At every depth `n ≥ 1` the\nweight-`n` Goncharov period filtration is non-empty.\n\nThis is the content the three deleted `opaque` constants were standing in\nfor, and it is *derived*: `sharpness` gives a grouplike at depth `n`,\n`inclusion` carries it into `P_n`. Conditional on the class, as it must be —\nwhich is exactly what the constants were not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.GBDepthPeriodCorrespondence.volume_conjecture_under_keystone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.GBDepthPeriodCorrespondence.volume_conjecture_under_keystone","kind":"def","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gb-depth-period-correspondence.lean#L132-L144","doc":"**Conditional (downstream of the keystone).** Given the volume grouplike of\na hyperbolic 3-manifold at depth 2, its archimedean realization is a period\nin `P_2` — the Volume-Conjecture-shaped consequence.\n\n`vg` is a hypothesis rather than an `opaque` constant for the same reason as\nabove: an `opaque` function INTO `GroupLikeDepth q 2` asserts that type is\ninhabited just as a constant does. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.GBDepthPeriodCorrespondence.Hyperbolic3Manifold","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.GBDepthPeriodCorrespondence.Hyperbolic3Manifold","kind":"opaque","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gb-depth-period-correspondence.lean#L129-L130","doc":"A hyperbolic 3-manifold. Placeholder. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.GBDepthPeriodCorrespondence.bring_trilog_zeta5_depth_3_under_keystone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.GBDepthPeriodCorrespondence.bring_trilog_zeta5_depth_3_under_keystone","kind":"def","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gb-depth-period-correspondence.lean#L121-L127","doc":"**Conditional (downstream of the keystone).** Same at depth 3, for the\nBring trilogarithm row `Li_3^q(ζ_5)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.GBDepthPeriodCorrespondence.figure_eight_depth_2_under_keystone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.GBDepthPeriodCorrespondence.figure_eight_depth_2_under_keystone","kind":"def","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gb-depth-period-correspondence.lean#L111-L119","doc":"**Conditional (downstream of the keystone).** Under the keystone class, a\ndepth-2 grouplike — e.g. the figure-8 row's `Li_2^q(ζ_6)`, verified\nnumerically in `conj:bring-figure-eight-depth-2-witness` — archimedean-\nrealizes to a period in `P_2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.GBDepthPeriodCorrespondence.GBDepthPeriodCorrespondence.sharpness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.GBDepthPeriodCorrespondence.GBDepthPeriodCorrespondence.sharpness","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gb-depth-period-correspondence.lean#L78-L78","doc":"Sharpness: at every depth `n ≥ 1`, the depth-`n` grouplike\nsub-Hopf-algebra is non-empty — there exists a grouplike at\ndepth `n` (which, by the inclusion, has a non-trivial\nGoncharov-period image).  In K-theoretic terms (per\n`rem:k-theory-period-rosetta`), this is implied by Borel's\ntheorem on `K_{2n-1}^ind(F) ⊗ ℚ` for appropriate number\nfields `F`.\n\nPer Gemini PR #634 review: replaces previous vacuous\n`∀ n, n ≥ 1 → True` with `Nonempty (GroupLikeDepth q n)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.GBDepthPeriodCorrespondence.GBDepthPeriodCorrespondence.inclusion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.GBDepthPeriodCorrespondence.GBDepthPeriodCorrespondence.inclusion","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gb-depth-period-correspondence.lean#L65-L65","doc":"Inclusion: at every depth `n`, the archimedean realization\nof a depth-`n` grouplike is a weight-`n` Goncharov period.\nStated as a function `GroupLikeDepth q n → GoncharovPeriodFiltration n`\nper Gemini PR #634 review.\n\nThe full Lean formalisation asserts this map factors\ncompatibly with the depth filtration on grouplikes and the\nweight filtration on Goncharov periods. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.GBDepthPeriodCorrespondence.GBDepthPeriodCorrespondence.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.GBDepthPeriodCorrespondence.GBDepthPeriodCorrespondence.mk","kind":"ctor","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gb-depth-period-correspondence.lean#L56-L56","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.GBDepthPeriodCorrespondence.GBDepthPeriodCorrespondence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.GBDepthPeriodCorrespondence.GBDepthPeriodCorrespondence","kind":"class","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gb-depth-period-correspondence.lean#L42-L79","doc":"**Class `GBDepthPeriodCorrespondence`** — encodes the keystone\nconjecture as an axiom class.  An instance asserts:\n\n1. Inclusion: `tau_arch(G^{(n)}(H_q)) ⊆ P_n` for every `n ≥ 0`.\n2. Sharpness: image generates `P_n / P_{n-1}` non-trivially\n   (for each `n ≥ 1`, there exists a grouplike at depth `n`\n   whose archimedean image lies in `P_n` but not `P_{n-1}`).\n\nConjectural inputs: the inclusion and sharpness assertions.\nOnce Beilinson's conjectures + Borel's theorem are wired,\nsharpness becomes a theorem\n(`rem:k-theory-period-rosetta` — Borel's theorem on\n`K_{2n-1}^ind(F) ⊗ ℚ`).\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.GBDepthPeriodCorrespondence.ArchimedeanRealization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.GBDepthPeriodCorrespondence.ArchimedeanRealization","kind":"opaque","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gb-depth-period-correspondence.lean#L38-L40","doc":"The archimedean realization functor `tau_arch : H_q → C(Spec)`.\nPlaceholder. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.GBDepthPeriodCorrespondence.GoncharovPeriodFiltration","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.GBDepthPeriodCorrespondence.GoncharovPeriodFiltration","kind":"opaque","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gb-depth-period-correspondence.lean#L33-L36","doc":"Goncharov period filtration: `P_n ⊂ ℝ` is the algebra of\nweight-`n` Goncharov periods. Placeholder; eventually wired\nthrough Mathlib's planned periods API. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.GBDepthPeriodCorrespondence.GroupLikeDepth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.GBDepthPeriodCorrespondence.GroupLikeDepth","kind":"opaque","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gb-depth-period-correspondence.lean#L28-L31","doc":"Iterated-integral depth filtration on grouplikes:\n`G^{(n)}(H_q) ⊆ H_q` is the sub-Hopf-algebra generated by\n`{exp_q, log_q, Li_2^q, ..., Li_n^q}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.GBDepthPeriodCorrespondence.ConvolutionHopfAlgebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.GBDepthPeriodCorrespondence.ConvolutionHopfAlgebra","kind":"opaque","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gb-depth-period-correspondence.lean#L25-L26","doc":"The substrate convolution Hopf algebra `H_q`. Placeholder. ","signatureChunk":0}]}